  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/mastacembelus_greshoffi_en/",
      "html": "<p>Some time ago Mastacembelus greshoffi could be imported from the Congo. It is a spiny eel reaching approximately 35 cm in length.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/mastacembelus_greshoffi_en/",
      "html": "<p>Congo, Cingo River.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/mastacembelus_greshoffi_en/",
      "html": "<p>Mastacembelus greshoffi occurs over rocky bottoms in rivers and lakes, also in rapids.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/mastacembelus_greshoffi_en/",
      "html": "<p>The best food is meaty food, and they eat rather plenty of it. They like mosquito larvae, worms and also now and then a small fish. Therefore, tank mates that are not too small should be selected for their socialization in a community tank.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/mastacembelus_greshoffi_en/",
      "html": "<p>Spiny eels are intelligent fish and show a multiplicity of interesting behaviours. They can also become amazingly tame and then eat literally from the hand of their caregiver. A complete covering of the aquarium is important, since spiny eels rank among the \"escapee kings\" among aquarium fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/mastacembelus_greshoffi_en/",
      "html": "<p>With a little luck and smartness, breeding of this species should be possible; some relatives have already been bred successfully in aquaria.</p>"
    }
  ],
